[ TUND: THE TUNNEL OF FJCC68 FIGS. 15 AND 16, SEEN HEAD-ON.  WITHOUT
[ DEPTH CUEING MANY SEE A PYRAMID FROM ABOVE; WITH IT, A TUNNEL.
[ THE ARRAY IS LINEAR AND CANNOT DIVIDE, SO THE PERSPECTIVE IS COMPUTED
[ BY TUNSUB, A SUBROUTINE CALLED BY THE JSR ITEM BELOW.  IT READS DIAL 0
[ AS HOW FAR YOU HAVE FLOWN IN, AND REWRITES THE TUNNEL'S POINTS.
[ SHOW IT WITH:
[     VIEW (.19, -.556, 37777)!   FRONT AT THE MOUTH, THE FAR END 10:1
[     DSPLY (V.TUND)!
[     CLOCK (DIALS+1, DI.EX)!
[ DEPTH CUEING OFF:  VIEW (,,0)!      ON AGAIN:  VIEW (,,37777)!
V.TUND: TEXT /V.TUND/
        JSR (TUNSUB)
        IMG (TUNNEL)
        RET
